1142
00:54:50.470 --> 00:54:51.630
I had wondered about that.

1143
00:54:51.750 --> 00:54:57.470
I have to say, I wondered, did they have to drive back to David Wallace's house and pick

1144
00:54:57.470 --> 00:54:57.770
up her car?

1145
00:54:57.850 --> 00:54:58.770
You know what I think she did?

1146
00:54:58.770 --> 00:55:02.210
I think she sent Michael in a cab the next day to get her car.

1147
00:55:02.390 --> 00:55:04.950
I think she drank too much wine and...

1148
00:55:04.950 --> 00:55:07.090
Oh, well, that's for sure why Michael drove her.

1149
00:55:07.310 --> 00:55:11.190
But how she retrieved her car, I bet she made Michael go get it.

1150
00:55:11.330 --> 00:55:13.270
And then I bet Michael made Dwight go get it.

1151
00:55:14.310 --> 00:55:15.990
Exactly, exactly.

1152
00:55:16.470 --> 00:55:21.410
Well, moving on to the negotiation, my pocket soapbox got a lot of mail.

1153
00:55:21.590 --> 00:55:28.790
In support of my position, one of my favorites came from Melanie Vergara, who said,

1154
00:55:29.110 --> 00:55:35.810
Ladies, I feel so strongly about the symbology of pockets that I refuse to even consider buying

1155
00:55:35.810 --> 00:55:37.550
a wedding dress without pockets.

1156
00:55:37.550 --> 00:55:40.490
And I found the wedding dress of my dreaMs.

1157
00:55:40.490 --> 00:55:41.670
It has pockets.

1158
00:55:41.830 --> 00:55:43.370
She's going to wear it this year.

1159
00:55:43.570 --> 00:55:46.010
I mean, a wedding dress with pockets is pretty phenomenal.

1160
00:55:46.270 --> 00:55:46.410
Yeah.

1161
00:55:46.870 --> 00:55:51.470
Well, Kinney, who is a historian, wrote in and had a correction for us.

1162
00:55:51.790 --> 00:55:58.030
Kinney says, women had pockets throughout history until the 1800s, when for various complicated

1163
00:55:58.030 --> 00:56:01.510
and mostly sexist reasons, women lost their pockets.

1164
00:56:01.790 --> 00:56:04.770
So yes, the lack of pockets is a sexist thing.

1165
00:56:04.770 --> 00:56:08.210
But the 400 years ago thing is wrong.

1166
00:56:08.430 --> 00:56:10.010
It's more like 200.

1167
00:56:10.430 --> 00:56:14.190
Secondly, she says, corsets were not bad for you.

1168
00:56:14.350 --> 00:56:16.310
In fact, they gave you great back support.

1169
00:56:16.590 --> 00:56:22.010
The reason corsets hurt people today is because they either haven't broken them in the same way

1170
00:56:22.010 --> 00:56:26.270
you have to break in a stiff material shoe before they're comfortable or because they

1171
00:56:26.270 --> 00:56:27.390
are not fitted properly.

1172
00:56:27.390 --> 00:56:32.890
Because people today don't realize the absolute importance of a well-fitted corset and that

1173
00:56:32.890 --> 00:56:37.670
she would personally take a corset over a bra any day.

1174
00:56:38.230 --> 00:56:38.470
Wow.

1175
00:56:38.830 --> 00:56:40.230
It's a lot of information there.

1176
00:56:40.570 --> 00:56:42.590
Kinney, I could not love this letter more.

1177
00:56:42.810 --> 00:56:43.770
Thank you very much.

1178
00:56:43.930 --> 00:56:48.970
Although I do have to say, having worn many corsets for acting projects over the year,

1179
00:56:49.070 --> 00:56:50.330
perhaps they were ill-fitted.

1180
00:56:50.570 --> 00:56:51.970
I'm going to go ahead and take a bra.

1181
00:56:52.270 --> 00:56:54.010
You're going to take a bra over a corset?

1182
00:56:54.010 --> 00:56:57.410
I'm going to take a sports bra, if I'm being honeSt.

1183
00:56:57.710 --> 00:57:01.270
I don't even want any of the underwire if I can avoid it.

1184
00:57:01.470 --> 00:57:04.190
You're going to go uniboob and be fine with it.

1185
00:57:04.390 --> 00:57:05.110
Here's the thing.

1186
00:57:05.250 --> 00:57:10.330
When I get dressed in the mornings, I like to get dressed as if I might have to break

1187
00:57:10.330 --> 00:57:13.070
into a full sprint at some point in the day.

1188
00:57:13.310 --> 00:57:13.750
Okay?

1189
00:57:14.070 --> 00:57:15.710
Your panic button is ready.

1190
00:57:15.710 --> 00:57:18.030
If you need to run, if you need to haul ass.

1191
00:57:18.150 --> 00:57:18.330
Yeah.

1192
00:57:18.470 --> 00:57:19.590
I'm dressed for it.

1193
00:57:19.670 --> 00:57:22.290
If there's an apocalyptic event, I'm ready.

1194
00:57:22.290 --> 00:57:24.850
Men are naturally dressed this way.

1195
00:57:25.230 --> 00:57:30.290
Truly, a man could pretty much break into a sprint pretty easily, right?

1196
00:57:30.810 --> 00:57:34.950
Well, I want to survive end of times, a possible mugging.

1197
00:57:35.090 --> 00:57:35.790
I don't know.

1198
00:57:36.070 --> 00:57:40.030
So no corsets, no Spanx, no high heels for me.

1199
00:57:40.030 --> 00:57:46.710
I need to run to my bag of expired medication, my book bag with my protein bars,

1200
00:57:46.710 --> 00:57:51.350
my backpack with the solar panel so I can charge my phone.

1201
00:57:51.570 --> 00:57:52.030
It's full.

1202
00:57:52.310 --> 00:57:54.930
You know what I have in my emergency backpack, Angela?

1203
00:57:55.070 --> 00:58:02.010
We live in Southern California, but I have four of those foil blankets that you wrap around

1204
00:58:02.010 --> 00:58:05.750
yourself like for extreme cold temperature because you don't know.

1205
00:58:05.910 --> 00:58:10.890
You don't know the weather shift that's going to happen if a meteor hits the earth.

1206
00:58:10.890 --> 00:58:15.190
This is like that Jake Gyllenhaal movie, The Day After Tomorrow, where, you know, all of a sudden,

1207
00:58:15.450 --> 00:58:19.610
this like crazy arctic storm freezes all of New York City.

1208
00:58:20.090 --> 00:58:20.290
Right.

1209
00:58:20.430 --> 00:58:24.870
I would have a foil blanket for that, and I would have comfortable clothing with giant pockets.

1210
00:58:25.130 --> 00:58:27.270
I would be as ready as possible.

1211
00:58:27.490 --> 00:58:28.270
You see what I'm saying?

1212
00:58:28.270 --> 00:58:29.330
I can't wear a corset.

1213
00:58:29.550 --> 00:58:29.910
I do.

1214
00:58:30.230 --> 00:58:30.870
No, you can't.

1215
00:58:30.910 --> 00:58:31.870
You can't wear a corset.

1216
00:58:32.110 --> 00:58:37.370
Jenna, you know, my theory on all of this is like what they say about a bear attack.

1217
00:58:37.530 --> 00:58:40.170
You only have to run faster than one other person.

1218
00:58:40.170 --> 00:58:41.570
Oh, my God.

1219
00:58:42.370 --> 00:58:47.690
I only have to be faster than one other person in the pack, and I'll be okay.

1220
00:58:47.890 --> 00:58:50.430
It's so interesting they didn't use that quote in The Edge.

1221
00:58:51.650 --> 00:58:54.290
They went with what one man has done another can do.

1222
00:58:54.450 --> 00:58:56.310
But yours is also very inspiring.

1223
00:58:58.110 --> 00:58:58.630
Okay.

1224
00:58:58.930 --> 00:59:04.670
Well, Jenna, it was also during the negotiation that we discussed our love of Keanu Reeves

1225
00:59:04.670 --> 00:59:10.010
movies, and last week we found out that you have not been watching John Wick.

1226
00:59:10.630 --> 00:59:11.390
I'm so sorry.

1227
00:59:12.330 --> 00:59:19.030
Well, I guess there are a few Keanu Reeves slash The Office crossover connections.

1228
00:59:19.430 --> 00:59:19.530
What?

1229
00:59:19.670 --> 00:59:22.790
Jenna, we are like six degrees separation of Keanu Reeves.

1230
00:59:22.950 --> 00:59:24.170
We almost know him.

1231
00:59:24.710 --> 00:59:24.930
What?

1232
00:59:25.330 --> 00:59:25.750
Ready?

1233
00:59:25.970 --> 00:59:27.650
Wait, I could blow your mind right now.

1234
00:59:27.930 --> 00:59:28.410
What?

1235
00:59:28.850 --> 00:59:29.970
Have you met him?

1236
